# RedCase — encoding enforcement (Addendum §8.5 encoding cleanup, 2026-09-22).
# Every text path is forced UTF-8 so the cp1252-mojibake class (â€" Â§ Â· â€™)
# cannot re-enter through git. Combined with .editorconfig's charset rule this is the
# CI/repo-level gate the Codebase Audit (H2) called for.

* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf charset=utf-8
*.ts text eol=lf charset=utf-8
*.tsx text eol=lf charset=utf-8
*.js text eol=lf charset=utf-8
*.json text eol=lf charset=utf-8
*.css text eol=lf charset=utf-8
*.md text eol=lf charset=utf-8
*.svg text=false
*.png binary
*.jpg binary

# text=auto normalizes on commit; these stop accidental CRLF/encoding churn on Windows.
